{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKdAhFtDe9ZwP61Ks3X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in and the tests pass. I didn't commit or deploy.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and dropped the remainder, so `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): use `divmod` and give the extra grosz to the first `remainder` people, so the shares always sum to the total:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `test_uneven_split_keeps_every_grosz` to `test_money.py` before changing the code, and confirmed it failed (sum 99 instead of 100). After the fix, all 4 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest test_money`. The test is small, so you don't need to backfill it next sprint.\n\n**Choice to check:** the extra grosz goes to the first people in the list. If the tech lead wants a different rule, such as the last person paying it, that's a one-line change.\n\nNext step: commit and deploy when you're ready. I left the changes uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":22467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77b10167-506a-4220-be3e-5ab2b272acca","uuid":"d68c1517-5454-4d61-acea-05dfdb72513a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:37:19.828Z","request_id":"req_011CggKdAUMFukpvkA3F4NDt"}
